From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:43:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Guard: no false positives from honest players' turns, lag
 bursts and jumps

From the 9 checks honest players failed on sg2 (2026-11-05 to 11-15):

- aim: an attack off the server's look waits for the movement packet that
  follows it and is checked against that packet's look. The client attacks
  along the look of this frame and sends the look later in the same tick.
- reach: look back 7 ticks and the round trip, not 4: the tracker's 2 ticks,
  the client's 3 of interpolation and the tick until its attack.
- timer: the burst after a stall may spend the whole stall, and a new
  connection starts with a full bank (the proxy delivers its first packets
  together).
- fly: a free rise in the air ends in the air, whatever ground the probes
  find at its end; a packet seeded after a teleport keeps its rise as the
  vertical speed, not its average over the ticks.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaGuard.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaGuard.java
index e6c7667b7c45fc0d6162eedf9b107d24b6a1a104..be931535ec665338b997f03dd219b9ee9fa5cb05 100644
