      * side of where the attacker was looking.
+     *
+     * <p>Where it was looking is not known yet when the hit is off to the side of the last look. The
+     * client turns its head every frame and attacks along that look, but sends the look only later in
+     * the same tick, after the attack (Minecraft.runTick: clickMouse, then the world's entities, the
+     * player's movement packet last): the server's yaw is a tick old. A player who turns quickly onto
+     * someone and hits in the same tick - 64 and 88 degrees in one tick were seen from honest players -
+     * hit off the server's look. Such a hit waits for the movement packet that follows it, and is
+     * checked against that packet's look (AIM_LATER; aimOkLater).
      */
